{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1548446-what-are-some-common-ptc-pitfalls-for-new-storytellers-to-look-out-for","id":1548446,"title":"What are some common PtC pitfalls for new storytellers to look out for?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-02-12T12:39:56-08:00","id":1548446,"title":"What are some common PtC pitfalls for new storytellers to look out for?","content":"As the title suggests, my group decided to play PtC in the Great War setting, and I'll be running it. Haven't run this before, what are some things I should have prepared, what are some things I should look out for? Etc. <br /> <br /> How much time and energy should I put into each of my players pilgrimages? That's the big thing I'm worried about ATM, getting their character concepts and building a pilgrimage out of that. <br /> <br /> I haven't started doing any prep yet, just doing research for now and waiting for the characters to be done before I start prepping the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-12T22:16:59-08:00","id":1548461,"title":"","content":"The 5 questions on the core book are essential in building the Pilgrimages.<br /> If you have already a plot in mind try to put together each of the 10 roles so that they are the right ones for each stage of the plot (for example if there is a major conflict scene give a Soldier role to one pilgrimage at least)<br /> Use spontaneus Elpis vision to point players to their next role more aligned to the plot.<br /> <br /> Consider that the whole pilgrimage should outline a coherent story of a learning and growing being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-13T06:43:01-08:00","id":1548470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1548446-what-are-some-common-ptc-pitfalls-for-new-storytellers-to-look-out-for?p=1548461#post1548461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 5 questions on the core book are essential in building the Pilgrimages.<br /> If you have already a plot in mind try to put together each of the 10 roles so that they are the right ones for each stage of the plot (for example if there is a major conflict scene give a Soldier role to one pilgrimage at least)<br /> Use spontaneus Elpis vision to point players to their next role more aligned to the plot.<br /> <br /> Consider that the whole pilgrimage should outline a coherent story of a learning and growing being.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've given them each the five questions already, only one player has gotten back to me with a concept so far and they still need to answer the four questions. <br /> <br /> I'm waiting to define a plot until I have talked with my players and done a session zero, although I do have some historic battles I know I want them to be at, otherwise I'm \u200b\u200bstill just researching the war atm.<br /> <br /> Can you plot out the <i>whole</i> pilgrimage early on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-14T01:11:46-08:00","id":1548489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aendrinastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1548446-what-are-some-common-ptc-pitfalls-for-new-storytellers-to-look-out-for?p=1548470#post1548470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've given them each the five questions already, only one player has gotten back to me with a concept so far and they still need to answer the four questions.<br /> <br /> I'm waiting to define a plot until I have talked with my players and done a session zero, although I do have some historic battles I know I want them to be at, otherwise I'm \u200bstill just researching the war atm.<br /> <br /> Can you plot out the <i>whole</i> pilgrimage early on?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Rules as written you should define the 10 roles and the 7 universal milestones at the start, but i think there is nothing wrong in creating it during play.<br /> Consider that the game tells you that the player (but not the character) should know all the 10 roles, but in my game i ve decided to keep them secret, and the players liked it.<br /> Of course you cannot script every single step in synchro with the plot, player decisions are too unpredictable.<br /> That said, it s useful to know in which direction you want to send the story of each character, so i usually prepare a chapter for each important role that i know a player must complete, at the right moment i send Elpis vision to hint that the player should pick the Role, and when the player has switched i start the Role chapter arc.<br /> Some arc can be integrated in the main plot, others could be played at any time between main events","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-17T06:45:20-08:00","id":1548547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1548446-what-are-some-common-ptc-pitfalls-for-new-storytellers-to-look-out-for?p=1548489#post1548489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, Rules as written you should define the 10 roles and the 7 universal milestones at the start, but i think there is nothing wrong in creating it during play.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry you define 10 roles? Which ten? One from each refinement?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-17T08:33:47-08:00","id":1548549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aendrinastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1548446-what-are-some-common-ptc-pitfalls-for-new-storytellers-to-look-out-for?p=1548547#post1548547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry you define 10 roles? Which ten? One from each refinement?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pag 177 to 184 of the Core book gives the instructions to create a Pilgrimage.<br /> You should prepare the Roles and specific Universal Milestones of each player based on their answers of the five questions (pag 101)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-17T09:06:47-08:00","id":1548550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1548446-what-are-some-common-ptc-pitfalls-for-new-storytellers-to-look-out-for?p=1548549#post1548549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pag 177 to 184 of the Core book gives the instructions to create a Pilgrimage.<br /> You should prepare the Roles and specific Universal Milestones of each player based on their answers of the five questions (pag 101)</div> </div> </div> </div>Right what I'm asking is do you figure out the milestone for every refinement in the game, or just the four they need to go through?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-17T09:31:51-08:00","id":1548551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aendrinastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1548446-what-are-some-common-ptc-pitfalls-for-new-storytellers-to-look-out-for?p=1548550#post1548550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right what I'm asking is do you figure out the milestone for every refinement in the game, or just the four they need to go through?</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither. Prescribed Milestones like those used to determine if a Role has been completed are come up with during play based on the character's actions and personality. Chapter Seven goes over the process of creating a Pilgrimage from a Storytelling perspective, on pages 296-303 (Prescribed Milestones in particular being discussed on pages 299-300).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-18T03:49:33-08:00","id":1548561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aendrinastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1548446-what-are-some-common-ptc-pitfalls-for-new-storytellers-to-look-out-for?p=1548550#post1548550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right what I'm asking is do you figure out the milestone for every refinement in the game, or just the four they need to go through?</div> </div> </div> </div>I prepare in advance only some of the Roles on Pilgrimage Milestones, mostly the ones that corresponds to main events in the main plot.<br /> For the other Roles i decide that they have been completed by talking to the player, like a character &quot;inner monologue&quot;, if the player comes to a realization and we are both satisfied by the scene then &quot;boom&quot; Vitriol exp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-18T15:41:29-08:00","id":1548573,"title":"","content":"I think I'm going to need to get my PCs made and then come back to this, because right now I feel like it isn't making sense to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-19T22:06:52-08:00","id":1548607,"title":"","content":"Okay, I understand my confusion. The four refinements confused me, I thought you just had to have four refinements with one role each, but you need to select a total of 10 and then complete 8 of them yeah? Am I understanding that correctly?<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>In order to complete the Great Work, a character has to internalize lessons from at least four Refinements \u2014 two basic Refinements and two complex Refinements.</b> Part of internalizing the lesson involves completing a Role in those Refinements (the character must master eight Roles in all, divided among the Refinements in her Pilgrimage in any arrangement).&quot;<br /> <br /> The bold part is what i was remembering from a year ago when we were thinking about giving PtC a try, i forgot the rest of that.<br /> <br /> So the Roles are; select 10, with at least 2 basic and at least 2 advanced, you can't do more advanced than you do basic, and at least 8 of the 10 Roles need to be completed. Am I understanding correctly now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-19T22:49:22-08:00","id":1548608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aendrinastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1548446-what-are-some-common-ptc-pitfalls-for-new-storytellers-to-look-out-for?p=1548607#post1548607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I understand my confusion. The four refinements confused me, I thought you just had to have four refinements with one role each, but you need to select a total of 10 and then complete 8 of them yeah? Am I understanding that correctly?<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>In order to complete the Great Work, a character has to internalize lessons from at least four Refinements \u2014 two basic Refinements and two complex Refinements.</b> Part of internalizing the lesson involves completing a Role in those Refinements (the character must master eight Roles in all, divided among the Refinements in her Pilgrimage in any arrangement).&quot;<br /> <br /> The bold part is what i was remembering from a year ago when we were thinking about giving PtC a try, i forgot the rest of that.<br /> <br /> So the Roles are; select 10, with at least 2 basic and at least 2 advanced, you can't do more advanced than you do basic, and at least 8 of the 10 Roles need to be completed. Am I understanding correctly now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it s correct<br /> Consider also that the character must complete all the Universal milestones tailored on its Pilgrimage","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 02-20-2025, 01:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-20T10:39:17-07:00","id":1550287,"title":"","content":"I return! I have gathered useful information from my two players and just want some insight into how to turn this information into a fun Pilgrimage for the characters.<br /> <br /> So both characters are Frankenstiens.<br /> <br /> The first character has selected the following roles: Martyr, Psychopomp, Confessor, Outcast, Follower, Hermit, Vigilante, Warden, Scientist, Daredevil and is starting out as a Psychopomp. His answers to the 5 questions are:<br /> What sort of human do you want to be?<br /> A serial killer who \u201csaves\u201d people by giving them a good death.<br /> <br /> How have humans taught you to fear and hate?<br /> Trench warfare<br /> <br /> How did you split with your creator?<br /> Murder. I read his favorite book, which was about a serial killer, decided to kill him so he could experience his favorite story.<br /> <br /> What keeps you on the Pilgrimage?<br /> Discovering the perfect ending for yourself<br /> <br /> What would give up to become human?<br /> My life.<br /> <br /> Lastely I asked both players to tell me a little bit about the bodies that make them up. This first player decided to be made of two lovers, their hearts are stitched together and part of the woman's brain has been placed inside the skull of the man, giving the character a third hemisphere. Otherwise he is a patchwork of their bodies put together, he described it as, &quot;the woman's tricept is connected to the man's arm, two of the fingers on the right hand are the man's, the rest are the woman's, etc.&quot;<br /> <br /> The second character selected these roles:<br /> Savage -&gt; Outcast -&gt; Pilgrim -&gt; Martyr -&gt; Deviant -&gt; Warden<br /> (Daredevil) (Observer, Leader, Envoy)<br /> \u200bBoth players took Daredevil because we agreed that a fighter piolet story where they both had that role could be fun. He is starting in Savage and wanted to progress through the 6 roles in order, with daredevil left out of the order for when the air combat story starts, and the other three being slotted in whereever along the way.<br /> He answered the 5 questions<br /> What sort of human do you want to be?<br /> A person that has given up on ambition and power in favor of being a kind moral person.<br /> <br /> How have humans taught you to fear and hate?<br /> They punish me for who I was, without regard for who I am now.<br /> <br /> How did you split with your creator?<br /> Set his house on fire with a thrown Molotov cocktail I concocted from flammable liquid he kept in his lab (where he kept me chained up). Used the distraction and chaos to smash the chain keeping me on the wall and escape (still attached to my neck).<br /> <br /> What keeps you on the Pilgrimage?<br /> Overcoming the actions of my pre-Promethean life<br /> <br /> What would give up to become human?<br /> My face<br /> <br /> He gave me an interesting character concept, his body is made up of the victims of a bomb attack put back together with the head of Franz Ferdinand on top of it all, an attempt by an Austrian alchemist to resurrect the slain hier to the empire.<br /> <br /> I know that I plan to have the ghosts of the people that were killed haunting the characters. So the first character would be haunted by the couple his body is made of, and the second character would be haunted by Franz and an amalgamation of ghosts that had been killed by a bomb in the Balkins. I also am toying with the idea of the first character having to deal with his creator after the creator has come back as a Sineater, but am not completely convinced of this plot thread.<br /> <br /> Anyway, how do I think about this information and turn it into a Pilgrimage?<br /> <br /> I already have a vague idea for the first role of each. Both players gave me a list of NPCs that they already know in the trenches. One of the NPCs the psychopomp gave me will be wounded and the created will have to decide to save him or let him die, thus letting him come to terms with his own ability to influence life and death. The savage has three NPCs that are trying to get close to him, at somepoint I'll give him an opportunity to lash out and harm them, letting him see what he is as a savage. Other than that, I'm not really sure how to map these things out, or even how to set these stories up in an interesting way.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-21T06:00:17-07:00","id":1550300,"title":"","content":"I think Ghosts can be tied thematically to the would-be Psychopomp's journey. How will they respond faced with people who didn't die all the way? Are they a sign of a &quot;bad&quot; death? Are they in need of a &quot;good&quot; death? This can spur thoughts on what a proper death needs to be like in addition to the killing itself. Maybe you could play out a funeral, for someone the character knew, with mourners listing all the reasons why the deceased should have lived, or being <i>relieved</i> that their suffering is over. A similar concept can be implemented by introducing an NPC with a &quot;bucket list&quot; - someone at the end of their life, be it through age or sickness, who wants to complete some milestones before their life ends. A later twist could be that they can be saved and want to be. Based on why they killed their creator, the PC has no idea why people want things, so let him learn about that and misinterpret it.<br /> <br /> The Savage is trickier for me, but perhaps their first step is to acknowledge that to do good, you need the (social) power to do good. Give them opportunities to improve the lot of other people, that their reliance on Savagery will undermine. The character seems to want to make a clean cut from the life of his &quot;donors&quot;, to the point of self-sabotage. Or maybe they should learn an opposite lesson - that freedom from society and from expectations of power is worth becoming a selfish and cruel person.<br /> <br /> In general, I think that in addition to giving PCs missions from different sources, you can simply offer them moral dilemmas and see what they do. Figure out what contradictory values they hold. At least, if the players are sold on the psychological aspect of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-21T22:53:31-07:00","id":1550311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aendrinastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1548446-what-are-some-common-ptc-pitfalls-for-new-storytellers-to-look-out-for?p=1550287#post1550287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I return! I have gathered useful information from my two players and just want some insight into how to turn this information into a fun Pilgrimage for the characters.<br /> <br /> So both characters are Frankenstiens.<br /> <br /> The first character has selected the following roles: Martyr, Psychopomp, Confessor, Outcast, Follower, Hermit, Vigilante, Warden, Scientist, Daredevil and is starting out as a Psychopomp. His answers to the 5 questions are:<br /> What sort of human do you want to be?<br /> A serial killer who \u201csaves\u201d people by giving them a good death.<br /> <br /> How have humans taught you to fear and hate?<br /> Trench warfare<br /> <br /> How did you split with your creator?<br /> Murder. I read his favorite book, which was about a serial killer, decided to kill him so he could experience his favorite story.<br /> <br /> What keeps you on the Pilgrimage?<br /> Discovering the perfect ending for yourself<br /> <br /> What would give up to become human?<br /> My life.<br /> <br /> Lastely I asked both players to tell me a little bit about the bodies that make them up. This first player decided to be made of two lovers, their hearts are stitched together and part of the woman's brain has been placed inside the skull of the man, giving the character a third hemisphere. Otherwise he is a patchwork of their bodies put together, he described it as, &quot;the woman's tricept is connected to the man's arm, two of the fingers on the right hand are the man's, the rest are the woman's, etc.&quot;<br /> <br /> The second character selected these roles:<br /> Savage -&gt; Outcast -&gt; Pilgrim -&gt; Martyr -&gt; Deviant -&gt; Warden<br /> (Daredevil) (Observer, Leader, Envoy)<br /> Both players took Daredevil because we agreed that a fighter piolet story where they both had that role could be fun. He is starting in Savage and wanted to progress through the 6 roles in order, with daredevil left out of the order for when the air combat story starts, and the other three being slotted in whereever along the way.<br /> He answered the 5 questions<br /> What sort of human do you want to be?<br /> A person that has given up on ambition and power in favor of being a kind moral person.<br /> <br /> How have humans taught you to fear and hate?<br /> They punish me for who I was, without regard for who I am now.<br /> <br /> How did you split with your creator?<br /> Set his house on fire with a thrown Molotov cocktail I concocted from flammable liquid he kept in his lab (where he kept me chained up). Used the distraction and chaos to smash the chain keeping me on the wall and escape (still attached to my neck).<br /> <br /> What keeps you on the Pilgrimage?<br /> Overcoming the actions of my pre-Promethean life<br /> <br /> What would give up to become human?<br /> My face<br /> <br /> He gave me an interesting character concept, his body is made up of the victims of a bomb attack put back together with the head of Franz Ferdinand on top of it all, an attempt by an Austrian alchemist to resurrect the slain hier to the empire.<br /> <br /> I know that I plan to have the ghosts of the people that were killed haunting the characters. So the first character would be haunted by the couple his body is made of, and the second character would be haunted by Franz and an amalgamation of ghosts that had been killed by a bomb in the Balkins. I also am toying with the idea of the first character having to deal with his creator after the creator has come back as a Sineater, but am not completely convinced of this plot thread.<br /> <br /> Anyway, how do I think about this information and turn it into a Pilgrimage?<br /> <br /> I already have a vague idea for the first role of each. Both players gave me a list of NPCs that they already know in the trenches. One of the NPCs the psychopomp gave me will be wounded and the created will have to decide to save him or let him die, thus letting him come to terms with his own ability to influence life and death. The savage has three NPCs that are trying to get close to him, at somepoint I'll give him an opportunity to lash out and harm them, letting him see what he is as a savage. Other than that, I'm not really sure how to map these things out, or even how to set these stories up in an interesting way.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is unusual for a new Promethean to start with a Complex refinement (the first one whith a Role from Phosphorus).<br /> There is an in game &quot;normal&quot; reason (he found an Athanor that teached the Refinement) or it is an oddity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T12:54:26-07:00","id":1550459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1548446-what-are-some-common-ptc-pitfalls-for-new-storytellers-to-look-out-for?p=1550300#post1550300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Ghosts can be tied thematically to the would-be Psychopomp's journey. How will they respond faced with people who didn't die all the way? Are they a sign of a &quot;bad&quot; death? Are they in need of a &quot;good&quot; death? This can spur thoughts on what a proper death needs to be like in addition to the killing itself. Maybe you could play out a funeral, for someone the character knew, with mourners listing all the reasons why the deceased should have lived, or being <i>relieved</i> that their suffering is over. A similar concept can be implemented by introducing an NPC with a &quot;bucket list&quot; - someone at the end of their life, be it through age or sickness, who wants to complete some milestones before their life ends. A later twist could be that they can be saved and want to be. Based on why they killed their creator, the PC has no idea why people want things, so let him learn about that and misinterpret it.<br /> <br /> The Savage is trickier for me, but perhaps their first step is to acknowledge that to do good, you need the (social) power to do good. Give them opportunities to improve the lot of other people, that their reliance on Savagery will undermine. The character seems to want to make a clean cut from the life of his &quot;donors&quot;, to the point of self-sabotage. Or maybe they should learn an opposite lesson - that freedom from society and from expectations of power is worth becoming a selfish and cruel person.<br /> <br /> In general, I think that in addition to giving PCs missions from different sources, you can simply offer them moral dilemmas and see what they do. Figure out what contradictory values they hold. At least, if the players are sold on the psychological aspect of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I was originally planning to use the Ghosts for the Savage character being he has some of the refinment of silver he is going to be going through, but you are right, they fit into the ideas of a good death really <i>really</i> well also! I have some ideas for that now, thank you!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1548446-what-are-some-common-ptc-pitfalls-for-new-storytellers-to-look-out-for?p=1550311#post1550311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is unusual for a new Promethean to start with a Complex refinement (the first one whith a Role from Phosphorus).<br /> There is an in game &quot;normal&quot; reason (he found an Athanor that teached the Refinement) or it is an oddity?</div> </div> </div> </div>He took his creator into the catacombs of Paris after he murdered him and while down there discovered an Anathor. It makes sense for what he wants to do with his character, so I offered that explination to him to use and he agreed, so he is starting in Phosphorus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}